# AbuseGuard whitelist
# One IP or CIDR per line. Lines starting with '#' are comments.
# Any address matched here is NEVER banned and NEVER reported.
#
# Panel edits apply immediately. After editing this file by hand, run:
#   sudo ag --policy-apply
# to validate the file and update fail2ban ignoreip + the kernel intel
# exception together (otherwise the change waits for the next 6h cycle).
#
# Loopback is always safe to keep:
127.0.0.0/8
::1
#
# Add your own trusted IPs / CIDRs below, e.g.:
# 203.0.113.10
# 198.51.100.0/24
